'''Cadaqués''' (pronunciation: {{W|IPA|[kəðəˈkes]}}; {{Langx|arn|Ñüngkakura|4=pointed rock}}) is the most populous [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Cerdanya]], within [[Balisca]]. It borders [[Dríadas]] to the west, [[Muntanya]] to the southwest and the [[Sea of Shuainia]] to the north. The region's name is a [[W:Corruption (linguistics)|corruption]] of the [[Volisanian language|Volisanian]] phrase ''Cap de Quers'' ("cape of rocks").

Originally dependent on [[Agriculture, forestry, and fishing in Balisca|agriculture, fishing]] and [[W:Trade|trade]], Cadaqués pioneered [[W:Industrialization|industrialization]] in Balisca and was transformed into a manufacturing center during the {{W|Industrial Revolution}}. During the 20th century, the economy of Cadaqués [[Cadaqués Miracle|shifted from manufacturing to services]], and in the 21st century, Cadaqués has emerged as a global leader in [[W:Biotechnology|biotechnology]], [[W:Engineering|engineering]], [[List of colleges and universities in Cerdanya|higher education]], [[W:Alternative finance|alternative finance]], and [[W:Maritime trade|maritime trade]].

